<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">North India</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">North <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> is the northern region of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-subcontinent">Indian subcontinent</a>, including the Indo-Gangetic plain. It has been the heartland of successive empires based at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agra">Agra</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babur">Babur</a> exploited its political fragmentation and the weakness of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> to found the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a> in 1526.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/north-india.jpg" alt="North India" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yann; edited by Jim Carter · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Taj_Mahal_(Edited).jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
